 ```
 
+### Compound Format
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h30m"
+ms(-5400000, { compound: true })      // "-1h30m"
+ms(91800000, { compound: true })      // "25h30m"
+```
+
+Output is compatible with Go's `time.ParseDuration`: no spaces between parts,
+hours are the largest unit (no `d`), and seconds the smallest. Leftover
+milliseconds are dropped (values under 1 second give `"0s"`). Takes precedence
+over `long`.
+
 ### Input Formats (Units)
 
 ```ts
